  "title": "Mine and yours",
  "goal": "Use benim, senin, onun… and leave them out when the suffix says it all.",
  "points": ["gp-genitive", "gp-genitive-possessive"],
  "intro": {
    "text": "The pronouns have a genitive too: *benim, senin, onun, bizim, sizin, onların*. *Benim* and *bizim* are irregular. With them the owned thing takes the owner's person: *benim çantam*, *senin ceketin*. Usually the suffix alone is enough: *çantam* (my bag).",
    "see": "gp-genitive"
  },
